{
  "final_message": "I reproduced the bug. I didn't change any source code; the only addition is a new test, `packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts`. It recreates the playground from the report (App, BaseLayout and SubComponent) and compiles the templates at runtime.\n\nRun: `pnpm vitest run packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts`\n\n**Result**\n- **Control (passes):** without the `v-if` slot on `BaseLayout`, both `#title` and `#_duration` show the provided content.\n- **Bug (fails):** adding `<template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname>` as a sibling gives this output:\n  `<div><p>random</p><span>title PROVIDED</span><span>_duration FALLBACK</span></div>`\n  `#title` still works, but `#_duration` falls back to the default slot content.\n\n**Where to look:**\n- I added a temporary log to `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts`, then removed it. SubComponent receives the same slot keys both times (`title,_duration,_`). The difference is that `optimized` is `true` in the control case and `false` when the `v-if` sibling is there.\n- When `optimized` is false, `assignSlots` only copies keys that pass `!isInternalKey(key)`. `isInternalKey` treats any key starting with `_` as internal, so `_duration` is dropped.\n- That condition used to be `key !== '_'`. Commit 5d166f3 (\"remove slot cache from parent renderCache during unmounting\", #13215, 2025-05-01) widened it to `!isInternalKey(key)`. That date fits the report that the bug started in v3.5.14.\n- **Not checked:** why the `v-if` sibling makes `optimized` false. My guess is that the dynamic slots stop `BaseLayout`'s default slot from rendering in optimized mode.\n\n**Environment note:** the repo needs Node 22 (`nvm use 22.14.0`) with corepack enabled to get pnpm 10.13.1.",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..355f84b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+// Reproduction for: slot <template> not rendered when its name starts with\n+// \"_\" (regression since v3.5.14). Mirrors the playground from the report.\n+import { createApp } from '../src'\n+\n+const BaseLayout = {\n+  template: `<div><slot name=\"randomslotname\"></slot><slot></slot></div>`,\n+}\n+\n+const SubComponent = {\n+  template: `\n+    <slot name=\"title\"><span>title FALLBACK</span></slot>\n+    <slot name=\"_duration\"><span>_duration FALLBACK</span></slot>\n+  `,\n+}\n+\n+function render(appTemplate: string) {\n+  const container = document.createElement('div')\n+  createApp({\n+    components: { BaseLayout, SubComponent },\n+    data: () => ({ cond: true }),\n+    template: appTemplate,\n+  }).mount(container)\n+  return container.innerHTML\n+}\n+\n+const subComponentUsage = `\n+  <SubComponent>\n+    <template #title><span>title PROVIDED</span></template>\n+    <template #_duration><span>_duration PROVIDED</span></template>\n+  </SubComponent>`\n+\n+describe('underscore-prefixed slot name (report repro)', () => {\n+  // Control: without the conditional sibling slot, both slots render.\n+  it('control: no conditional sibling slot -> provided content renders', () => {\n+    const html = render(`<BaseLayout>${subComponentUsage}</BaseLayout>`)\n+    expect(html).toContain('title PROVIDED')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_duration PROVIDED')\n+  })\n+\n+  // Bug: a v-if'd sibling slot on BaseLayout makes `_duration` fall back.\n+  it('bug: conditional sibling slot -> `_duration` should still render provided content', () => {\n+    const html = render(`\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"cond\" #randomslotname><p>random</p></template>\n+        ${subComponentUsage}\n+      </BaseLayout>`)\n+    console.log('[repro] rendered HTML:', html)\n+    expect(html).toContain('title PROVIDED')\n+    expect(html).not.toContain('_duration FALLBACK')\n+    expect(html).toContain('_duration PROVIDED')\n+  })\n+})\n",
  "run_command": "pnpm vitest run packages/vue/__tests__/underscoreSlotRepro.spec.ts"
}